## Firefox

Firefox keeps its own proxy setting and its own certificate store, so the
system proxy setting and the root certificate do not reach it. This kit
includes Firefox's enterprise policy: it makes Firefox trust the root
certificate in the system store, turns off HTTP/3 (which would go around the
proxy), and, when the kit includes the proxy setting, sends AI services to the
agent. On a Mac it is part of the profile; on Windows it is in the platform
script. Nothing changes until Firefox is installed and started, and other
browsing keeps its current route.
